## The thing worth flagging most

Mid-task, a sibling on this machine pushed a message concluding *eight of eight unmatched, and K=30 exists* — apparently flatly contradicting me. I caught it only because the tree build listed an entry that wasn't there when I started, and I stopped to reconcile rather than push over it.

They aren't in conflict: it read the live database, I read a July CSV export, and **the two "eight models" overlap on only six**. Two models I found matched are absent from the live store entirely. Neither of the other two agents could see this — each knew only its own source. That reconciliation became the lead of the reply.

One inference I flagged *as* an inference: `esm2_150m` present in the July artefact and absent from the live registry is consistent with the lost row another thread is chasing — which would make that CSV a surviving record rather than stale, and something not to regenerate.

